{"type":"step-attempt","step":"cross-boundary-invariants","sessionId":"04a94bf1-9067-4dd0-b0f5-4ed25f4bfdb8","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/code-fixer-critical-fallback/cross-boundary-invariants-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/step/code-fixer.test.ts","title":"Test describe block title claims 'all branches' but continuation paths are systematically excluded","rationale":"The describe block 'prompt severity contract: all branches must include HIGH and CRITICAL (mandatory)' covers 5 initial-entry branches but not the 3 continuation branches (which route to buildContinuationMessage and carry no severity language by design). The spec's definition of 'branches' matches the 5 tested, but the title could mislead a future maintainer into believing all 8 possible paths through buildMessage are covered. This could cause a missed regression if buildContinuationMessage were changed to start a new session context. The fix is to add a comment clarifying that continuation branches are intentionally excluded.","line":401}],"evidence":{"checked":7,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/code-fixer.ts","title":"Conformance initial-entry branch uses a slightly different severity phrase (pre-existing)","rationale":"The conformance branch says 'Fix all HIGH and CRITICAL severity findings from the conformance review (mandatory)' while all other branches say 'Fix all HIGH and CRITICAL severity findings (mandatory)'. The new tests use toContain() which matches both forms. This asymmetry predates the change and is not introduced by it.","line":148},{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/fixer-helpers.ts","title":"buildContinuationMessage carries no severity mandate — continuation sessions rely on session context","rationale":"Continuation paths (isFixerContinuation === true) route to buildContinuationMessage before the fallback branches are reached. buildContinuationMessage emits no 'HIGH and CRITICAL (mandatory)' instruction, relying on session memory from the initial-entry turn. This is a pre-existing design choice. The current change does not alter this behavior or introduce new risks.","line":180}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-07T12:04:27.537Z","endedAt":"2026-08-07T12:09:12.587Z"}
